  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSIRO Partnership for Public Health Outcomes in the Pacific &amp; Southeast Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This partnership commenced in FY 23/24 and this investment consists of three major components: 1. CSIRO will support the improved capacity to manufacture essential drugs and vaccines in Thailand &amp; Malaysia; 2. CSIRO will strengthen and enhance digital health capabilities in the Philippines &amp; Fiji; 3. CSIRO&apos;s Australian Centre for Disease Preparedness (ACDP) is delivering five subprojects to strengthen Indonesia&#x2019;s national avian influenza reference laboratory (DIC WATES) and selected ASEAN region animal health laboratories; conduct laboratory biosafety training for laboratory staff from the region; improve testing for emerging infectious diseases at high-risk wildlife, livestock, human interface locations in Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos and the Philippines; and boost field diagnostic networks in the Pacific.</narrative>
  </description>
